    "sanitizedNotes": "BUILD 35 — SUBMITTED REVIEW BUILD\nPlease review iOS App 1.0.0 (35), the binary attached to this submission. It supersedes previously withdrawn or test builds and contains the corrections submitted for review.\nNo purchase is required for review.\n\nSCREENSHOTS — GUIDELINE 2.3.10\nAll App Store screenshots have been replaced with current iOS-only screenshots. They accurately represent the submitted iOS Build 35 and contain no Android interface elements or non-iOS status bars.\n\nREVIEW ACCESS\nPlease use the private demo credentials provided in App Review Information. The reviewer account is email-confirmed and has server-managed Premium and AI Coach access. No in-app purchase or subscription is required.\nLaunch steps:\n1. Choose English.\n2. Complete the age step.\n3. Tap Sign in > Store reviewer access.\n4. Enter the supplied review credentials.\nCore local logging features can also be evaluated without signing in.\n\nTHIRD-PARTY AI PRIVACY — GUIDELINES 5.1.1(i) AND 5.1.2(i)\nAI Coach: After signing in, open More > AI Coach settings and enable Remote AI consent. Alternatively, submit a question in AI Coach to display the consent prompt. Before sending any remote AI request, BIL:\n- identifies Google Gemini as a third-party AI service operated by Google;\n- explains that the user’s question and only the selected relevant context categories may be sent;\n- states that raw microphone audio is not sent; and\n- requires the user to select Allow & Continue.\nSelect Don’t Allow to verify that consent is not recorded and no request is sent to Google Gemini. Local and manual features remain available. Consent can be withdrawn later under More > AI Coach settings.\n\nMeal-photo analysis: Open Food Log > Analyze meal photo. Before image selection or upload, BIL separately:\n- identifies Google Gemini as a third-party AI service operated by Google;\n- explains that the selected image, locale, and minimum request metadata are sent to suggest visible foods; and\n- requires the user to select Allow & Continue.\nSelect Don’t Allow to return without selecting or sending an image. No image is uploaded and no food is logged until the user grants consent, reviews the suggested results, and confirms them. Consent can be withdrawn under More > Sharing & Privacy.\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION\nReferences, methodology, and limitations are available under:\nMore > Settings > Health preferences > Health sources & methodology\nBIL is a wellness application and does not diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent medical conditions.\n\nHEALTHKIT\nHealth data read permissions are optional and requested separately for each supported data type. Weight export is separate, user-initiated, and requires Health write permission.\n\nACCOUNT DELETION\nIn-app path: More > Help > Delete Account\nPrivacy Policy: https://www.bilhealth.com/privacy\nAccount Deletion: https://www.bilhealth.com/account-deletion\nSupport: https://www.bilhealth.com/support",
    "privateFieldComparisonEvidence": "Presence booleans here; equality booleans after mutation. No credential-derived hash retained."
